<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose 11 points to 1,311.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose 11 points to 1,311.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,311 today from 1,300 on June 26, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates</p>
<p>in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1383    12.556	  1376    12.494</p>
<p>   1a   1322 10013.000	  1315  9963.000</p>
<p>   2    1563    22.331	  1541    22.013</p>
<p>   2a   1557 12769.000	  1538 12613.000</p>
<p>   3    1363    12.575	  1354    12.488</p>
<p>   3a   1204  9500.000	  1195  9431.000</p>
<p>   6    1286    13.269	  1284    13.244</p>
